1
00:00:03,145 --> 00:00:08,027
Welcome to School O S. In this walkthrough,
we’ll take a school from its

2
00:00:08,041 --> 00:00:12,457
first sign-in to a connected school day:
teachers with the right access,

3
00:00:12,715 --> 00:00:17,348
pupils in the right classes, families
connected, and the services your school

4
00:00:17,361 --> 00:00:21,954
actually uses ready to work. You don’t need
to turn on every feature.

5
00:00:22,375 --> 00:00:26,886
We’ll start with six foundations, then
prepare fees, attendance,

6
00:00:27,144 --> 00:00:32,130
communication and reports. Transport,
boarding, the library

7
00:00:32,144 --> 00:00:35,079
and the school store each have their own
optional chapter.

8
00:00:35,514 --> 00:00:38,149
We’re using fictional training records.

9
00:00:38,557 --> 00:00:43,136
When you set up your school, use your
approved school records and verify each

10
00:00:43,149 --> 00:00:45,255
connection before sharing access.

11
00:00:45,690 --> 00:00:50,174
You can pause at any chapter, complete that
step, and return here.

12
00:01:00,686 --> 00:01:04,626
Start with the access details issued for
your own school account.

13
00:01:05,065 --> 00:01:09,644
If you receive a password-setup link, open
it privately and choose your own

14
00:01:09,658 --> 00:01:13,489
password. Never share the owner’s login
with staff.

15
00:01:13,924 --> 00:01:18,217
After signing in, check that the school
name and your role are correct.

16
00:01:18,639 --> 00:01:21,546
Start my school guides the initial setup.

17
00:01:21,967 --> 00:01:24,753
My school day brings together daily work.

18
00:01:25,160 --> 00:01:29,671
More tools is the organised directory you
can return to whenever you need a

19
00:01:29,685 --> 00:01:34,318
particular service. For help with a step,
open Show me around.

20
00:01:34,753 --> 00:01:38,815
Where voice guidance is available, select
Listen to this step.

21
00:01:39,250 --> 00:01:41,492
You can stop the voice at any time.

22
00:01:41,927 --> 00:01:46,709
If you belong to the wrong school, or your
access link has expired, stop here and

23
00:01:46,723 --> 00:01:48,679
ask for a corrected invitation.

24
00:01:49,070 --> 00:01:51,665
Don’t continue inside the wrong account.

25
00:02:02,190 --> 00:02:05,206
Let’s give this workspace its school
identity.

26
00:02:05,618 --> 00:02:09,640
If Prepare my school workspaces is shown,
use it first.

27
00:02:10,075 --> 00:02:14,803
Then enter the school’s official name,
contact address, phone number and

28
00:02:14,817 --> 00:02:18,634
email. Use an address the school actually
monitors.

29
00:02:19,069 --> 00:02:23,933
These details help families recognise your
school and know where to ask for help.

30
00:02:24,341 --> 00:02:29,083
In this recording, the contact details are
controlled training details.

31
00:02:29,490 --> 00:02:34,042
Select Save school details. Wait for the
confirmation, then

32
00:02:34,056 --> 00:02:37,466
reopen the step and check that the
information is still there.

33
00:02:37,901 --> 00:02:42,846
A click on Save is only the beginning;
seeing the saved record again tells us the

34
00:02:42,860 --> 00:02:47,507
change was retained. If your school has
more than one site, keep the

35
00:02:47,520 --> 00:02:49,613
organisation’s identity clear.

36
00:02:50,034 --> 00:02:52,996
We’ll deal with branches and access
separately.

37
00:03:03,526 --> 00:03:06,080
Now let’s make the school recognisable.

38
00:03:06,492 --> 00:03:11,085
Open Logo, colours and document branding,
and edit the existing

39
00:03:11,098 --> 00:03:13,598
branding record if one is already present.

40
00:03:14,033 --> 00:03:18,884
Upload your school logo. Use a clear PNG,
JPEG or

41
00:03:18,897 --> 00:03:21,316
WebP file within the upload limit.

42
00:03:21,707 --> 00:03:26,626
Choose colours that work with readable
text, and review the motto, website

43
00:03:26,735 --> 00:03:31,207
and contact details. Save the record, then
open it again to

44
00:03:31,221 --> 00:03:33,177
confirm the logo and colours.

45
00:03:33,612 --> 00:03:38,259
Later, when we open a printable report,
we’ll check the actual document

46
00:03:38,272 --> 00:03:42,701
too. Saving a logo here doesn’t replace
that final check.

47
00:03:43,092 --> 00:03:47,304
Keep the school name consistent across the
profile, branding and

48
00:03:47,318 --> 00:03:51,941
documents. Families should immediately
recognise that they are looking at their

49
00:03:51,954 --> 00:03:53,517
own school’s information.

50
00:04:04,060 --> 00:04:08,095
A small school shouldn’t have to operate
like a large institution.

51
00:04:08,507 --> 00:04:12,080
Open Roles and permissions, then School
services.

52
00:04:12,515 --> 00:04:17,094
If this is the first visit, prepare the
roles and permissions workspace.

53
00:04:17,485 --> 00:04:20,474
The small-school selection is a starting
point.

54
00:04:20,912 --> 00:04:25,895
Review it before saving. Keep the services
your school needs now, and add

55
00:04:25,908 --> 00:04:30,786
transport, boarding, a library or other
services when they become relevant.

56
00:04:31,180 --> 00:04:35,650
Turning a service off preserves its records
while limiting delegated

57
00:04:35,664 --> 00:04:39,091
use. It is not a way to delete school
history.

58
00:04:39,512 --> 00:04:44,376
Next, notice the difference between a role
template and a person’s access.

59
00:04:44,811 --> 00:04:47,624
A template describes a responsibility.

60
00:04:48,058 --> 00:04:52,923
It does not create an employee, issue a
login or automatically authorise

61
00:04:52,936 --> 00:04:57,895
someone to see records. We’ll connect those
pieces deliberately in the next

62
00:04:57,909 --> 00:04:58,507
steps.

63
00:05:09,057 --> 00:05:13,486
Your session, classes and subjects are the
structure that pupils,

64
00:05:13,772 --> 00:05:16,625
teachers, attendance and results depend on.

65
00:05:17,037 --> 00:05:21,534
Open the SmartStart assistant and choose
the school type and levels you actually

66
00:05:21,548 --> 00:05:26,521
operate. For this training school, we’re
using Primary classes, one

67
00:05:26,534 --> 00:05:31,263
class per year group, the twenty twenty-six
to twenty twenty-seven session, and

68
00:05:31,276 --> 00:05:36,032
First Term. If your school uses arms,
select the correct structure

69
00:05:36,045 --> 00:05:39,089
instead. Select Preview my setup.

70
00:05:39,496 --> 00:05:42,377
Read the proposed classes before approving.

71
00:05:42,811 --> 00:05:47,716
Starter subjects are optional, editable
examples; they are not a complete

72
00:05:47,730 --> 00:05:52,295
curriculum for every school. Approve the
setup and wait for the saved

73
00:05:52,309 --> 00:05:55,923
result. Now open Manage actual classes.

74
00:05:56,315 --> 00:06:00,187
Check that the real class records exist in
the correct session.

75
00:06:00,624 --> 00:06:03,083
Then check the actual subject list.

76
00:06:03,518 --> 00:06:06,928
The assessment pattern in the assistant is
a preference.

77
00:06:07,363 --> 00:06:11,888
We still need to configure the actual
assessments and report workflow before

78
00:06:11,901 --> 00:06:16,371
issuing results. And the preview itself is
not proof that records were

79
00:06:16,385 --> 00:06:20,692
created: the saved confirmation and the
reopened lists are what we

80
00:06:20,705 --> 00:06:21,398
verify.

81
00:06:31,945 --> 00:06:36,619
Before bringing real families into the
system, check the school calendar and the

82
00:06:36,633 --> 00:06:41,525
rules your team will use. Confirm the
current academic session, term

83
00:06:41,539 --> 00:06:44,623
dates and any calendar entries your school
needs.

84
00:06:45,018 --> 00:06:47,219
Use your school’s approved dates.

85
00:06:47,613 --> 00:06:50,113
Don’t copy dates from this tutorial.

86
00:06:50,536 --> 00:06:55,210
Review admission-number conventions and the
assessment policies that apply to each

87
00:06:55,224 --> 00:06:59,721
level. Some settings pages store
configuration, while working

88
00:06:59,735 --> 00:07:04,151
screens hold the actual classes,
assessments or report designs.

89
00:07:04,558 --> 00:07:07,955
We’ll verify those working records where
they are used.

90
00:07:08,363 --> 00:07:12,928
Also review who may access pupil
information, why the school holds it,

91
00:07:13,227 --> 00:07:17,629
how long it is retained and how corrections
or consent questions are handled.

92
00:07:18,064 --> 00:07:22,045
A saved acknowledgement is not a substitute
for the school’s privacy

93
00:07:22,058 --> 00:07:26,905
responsibilities. Complete that review
before real child data is

94
00:07:26,919 --> 00:07:27,938
brought on board.

95
00:07:38,462 --> 00:07:42,375
Let’s add a teacher without creating
disconnected records.

96
00:07:42,787 --> 00:07:47,257
Enter the teacher’s full name and select
Teacher as the working dashboard.

97
00:07:47,665 --> 00:07:52,271
An email address is optional here because
the school issues a sign-in ID.

98
00:07:52,705 --> 00:07:56,931
Where email is used, verify that it belongs
to the employee.

99
00:07:57,366 --> 00:08:02,216
If the person already has an HR or teacher-
directory record, connect that

100
00:08:02,230 --> 00:08:04,662
record instead of creating a duplicate.

101
00:08:05,083 --> 00:08:09,037
For a new employee, use the correct
employment start date.

102
00:08:09,429 --> 00:08:14,062
Confirm employment only when the person has
actually been approved to work and may

103
00:08:14,076 --> 00:08:18,317
clock in. Otherwise, leave that
confirmation for the HR

104
00:08:18,330 --> 00:08:23,045
process. Review the identity and access
confirmation, then

105
00:08:23,059 --> 00:08:25,165
create the connected staff login.

106
00:08:25,556 --> 00:08:27,825
Check the next steps for this person.

107
00:08:28,235 --> 00:08:32,678
Share access privately, and have the
teacher complete their own password

108
00:08:32,692 --> 00:08:37,379
setup. The teacher must use their own
account; they should never borrow the

109
00:08:37,393 --> 00:08:38,629
school owner’s login.

110
00:08:49,185 --> 00:08:54,144
Other staff follow the same principle:
start with a real person, then give that

111
00:08:54,158 --> 00:08:56,196
person a reviewed responsibility.

112
00:08:56,635 --> 00:08:59,774
Your school can activate only the jobs it
needs.

113
00:09:00,208 --> 00:09:04,556
One employee can hold more than one
responsibility on one login.

114
00:09:04,964 --> 00:09:08,510
Open the relevant role template and read
its permissions.

115
00:09:08,945 --> 00:09:13,714
Then find the employee in People and access
and preview their current access

116
00:09:13,728 --> 00:09:18,588
before adding anything. Choose whether the
responsibility covers the whole school

117
00:09:18,602 --> 00:09:22,624
or a supported set of classes, branches or
departments.

118
00:09:23,035 --> 00:09:26,798
A limited scope needs the matching scope
records selected.

119
00:09:27,219 --> 00:09:31,798
Some services require whole-school
authority; don’t assume every screen

120
00:09:31,812 --> 00:09:36,594
supports every scope. Financial approval is
a separate decision.

121
00:09:37,016 --> 00:09:40,358
A ceiling of zero means no financial
approvals.

122
00:09:40,766 --> 00:09:44,434
Give a higher amount only where the school
has authorised it.

123
00:09:44,855 --> 00:09:48,999
Save the reviewed responsibility, then test
the staff account.

124
00:09:49,391 --> 00:09:52,693
Check both what it can do and what it must
not see.

125
00:09:53,130 --> 00:09:57,994
A Principal can be given appropriate
financial visibility and follow-up duties

126
00:09:58,007 --> 00:10:01,323
without automatically receiving the owner’s
full authority.

127
00:10:11,881 --> 00:10:16,623
If the school already has a team, staff
invitations can reduce repeated

128
00:10:16,637 --> 00:10:21,587
data entry. Use the school’s staff-
invitation flow, collect the required

129
00:10:21,600 --> 00:10:26,288
details, and review each request against
employment records before granting

130
00:10:26,301 --> 00:10:30,282
access. An invitation is not employment
approval.

131
00:10:30,717 --> 00:10:35,404
A job title entered by an applicant is not
permission to open confidential

132
00:10:35,418 --> 00:10:40,333
records. Connect the verified person, their
employment record and

133
00:10:40,347 --> 00:10:42,059
their reviewed responsibility.

134
00:10:42,483 --> 00:10:47,443
For multiple branches, add the branch,
connect its classes and then review

135
00:10:47,456 --> 00:10:52,144
staff scope. A branch name saved in school
settings alone does not

136
00:10:52,157 --> 00:10:56,665
isolate records. Check the actual
permissions with separate staff

137
00:10:56,678 --> 00:11:01,627
accounts. If your school has one site and a
small team, you can keep this

138
00:11:01,641 --> 00:11:03,923
simple and return to branches later.

139
00:11:14,465 --> 00:11:19,193
A teacher login alone doesn’t connect a
teacher to pupils or subjects.

140
00:11:19,605 --> 00:11:24,198
Open Teacher allocation and choose the
class, subject, academic

141
00:11:24,211 --> 00:11:28,478
session and teacher. Save the allocation
and check the Current

142
00:11:28,491 --> 00:11:33,423
allocations table. Repeat this for every
class and subject that needs a

143
00:11:33,437 --> 00:11:38,056
teacher. One sample allocation can satisfy
part of the startup

144
00:11:38,070 --> 00:11:41,956
check, but it does not mean the whole
school has been staffed correctly.

145
00:11:42,391 --> 00:11:46,983
Next, open Timetable and place the lesson
in the correct class, with the

146
00:11:46,997 --> 00:11:50,584
correct teacher, day, start time and end
time.

147
00:11:51,005 --> 00:11:54,959
Review any conflict message instead of
forcing an overlap.

148
00:11:55,366 --> 00:12:00,040
Later, when the teacher signs in, we’ll
confirm that these are the classes they

149
00:12:00,054 --> 00:12:04,262
actually see. Keep sessions consistent
across class records,

150
00:12:04,480 --> 00:12:09,317
allocations, assessments and reports; a
mismatch can make a correctly

151
00:12:09,330 --> 00:12:11,273
saved record appear to be missing.

152
00:12:21,812 --> 00:12:26,503
Now return to Safe access. This step
records the school’s access

153
00:12:26,517 --> 00:12:30,552
plan, so read it rather than treating the
checkbox as a shortcut.

154
00:12:30,943 --> 00:12:35,291
Confirm that people use individual logins,
duties have been reviewed,

155
00:12:35,617 --> 00:12:40,250
sensitive information is restricted and
family connections will be checked before

156
00:12:40,264 --> 00:12:45,199
access is shared. If one of those
arrangements is not ready, leave the step

157
00:12:45,213 --> 00:12:49,859
open and fix it. When the plan is genuinely
in place, save

158
00:12:49,873 --> 00:12:54,493
it. The platform’s percentage reflects
saved setup checks.

159
00:12:54,927 --> 00:12:59,520
It is a helpful guide, not a certificate
that every permission, payment

160
00:12:59,533 --> 00:13:02,577
connection or teaching workflow has been
tested.

161
00:13:13,102 --> 00:13:15,249
There are two different situations.

162
00:13:15,661 --> 00:13:20,131
A pupil who already attends your school
needs an existing-family onboarding

163
00:13:20,144 --> 00:13:24,193
process. A new applicant needs an admission
decision.

164
00:13:24,614 --> 00:13:29,234
For existing families, the parent can
complete a school registration form with

165
00:13:29,248 --> 00:13:32,902
more than one child, or the school can add
the family manually.

166
00:13:33,324 --> 00:13:37,114
Staff then verify each child against the
school register.

167
00:13:37,549 --> 00:13:42,481
Don’t make an existing pupil apply as a new
admission just to receive a login.

168
00:13:42,916 --> 00:13:47,332
That can create duplicate records and
separate the child from their history.

169
00:13:47,767 --> 00:13:52,359
We’ll start with an existing family and
connect two children to one verified

170
00:13:52,373 --> 00:13:57,006
parent. If your school is bringing in many
records, test a small

171
00:13:57,019 --> 00:14:01,612
sample first. Use the application’s actual
import template where

172
00:14:01,625 --> 00:14:05,769
offered, and check classes and duplicates
before a full import.

173
00:14:16,313 --> 00:14:20,022
Here is the link the school can share with
existing families.

174
00:14:20,419 --> 00:14:24,796
Open Family onboarding. If the workspace
needs preparation,

175
00:14:25,095 --> 00:14:28,940
complete that first, then generate and
enable the school link.

176
00:14:29,347 --> 00:14:32,146
Check that the link is visible and marked
ready.

177
00:14:32,537 --> 00:14:35,485
Copy it and open the parent-form preview.

178
00:14:35,923 --> 00:14:40,597
In a separate browser, confirm that it
opens the intended school’s form with the

179
00:14:40,611 --> 00:14:45,529
correct identity. A paused link needs to be
enabled before families can

180
00:14:45,543 --> 00:14:49,999
submit. Replacing a public link makes the
old one stop accepting

181
00:14:50,013 --> 00:14:54,266
submissions, so don’t rotate it after
sharing without a clear reason.

182
00:14:54,701 --> 00:14:58,546
The shared demo cannot issue a live school
registration link.

183
00:14:58,967 --> 00:15:03,179
For this recording we’re using an isolated
normal training school.

184
00:15:03,614 --> 00:15:08,356
If your real link is blank or points to the
wrong address, ask the platform team

185
00:15:08,369 --> 00:15:11,752
to check the installation address before
sending it to families.

186
00:15:22,305 --> 00:15:24,316
The form belongs to this school.

187
00:15:24,742 --> 00:15:29,565
First, the parent enters their own name,
email, WhatsApp number and

188
00:15:29,578 --> 00:15:31,182
relationship to the children.

189
00:15:31,603 --> 00:15:33,899
Then they add each child separately.

190
00:15:34,334 --> 00:15:39,103
Here, one parent is registering two
children, so we add the first child,

191
00:15:39,375 --> 00:15:44,144
then the second. The details should help
the school find each child in its

192
00:15:44,157 --> 00:15:48,750
existing register. Before sending, check
spelling, contact

193
00:15:48,763 --> 00:15:50,815
details and the children listed.

194
00:15:51,236 --> 00:15:54,035
Submit the form and read the
acknowledgement.

195
00:15:54,456 --> 00:15:57,731
Submission does not automatically grant
access.

196
00:15:58,165 --> 00:16:02,812
The school still needs to verify identity,
guardian authority and the

197
00:16:02,826 --> 00:16:07,758
child’s record. This protects families and
prevents a person from claiming

198
00:16:07,771 --> 00:16:10,244
access just by knowing a pupil’s name.

199
00:16:10,679 --> 00:16:15,570
If a parent cannot complete an online form,
school staff can use Add a family

200
00:16:15,584 --> 00:16:18,722
manually and follow the same verification
process.

201
00:16:29,281 --> 00:16:33,982
This is the most important part of family
onboarding: connecting people to the

202
00:16:33,996 --> 00:16:38,756
right records. Open the family submission
and review each child.

203
00:16:39,190 --> 00:16:43,728
If the pupil already exists, search the
register and use the existing

204
00:16:43,742 --> 00:16:48,060
record. Check the admission number, class
and other school

205
00:16:48,074 --> 00:16:51,663
evidence. Don’t rely on a matching name
alone.

206
00:16:52,098 --> 00:16:56,867
If the pupil is genuinely missing, create a
verified record in the confirmed

207
00:16:56,881 --> 00:17:01,065
class and session, using the original
admission date where appropriate.

208
00:17:01,487 --> 00:17:04,516
Review possible duplicates before
continuing.

209
00:17:04,938 --> 00:17:08,742
Verify the parent’s authority and contact
details.

210
00:17:09,163 --> 00:17:12,804
Reuse the same verified parent account for
siblings.

211
00:17:13,196 --> 00:17:17,721
Choose a pupil login only where your school
intends that child to have one.

212
00:17:18,131 --> 00:17:21,962
Record the evidence and save the verified
match for approval.

213
00:17:22,370 --> 00:17:25,454
An authorised reviewer can then approve the
child.

214
00:17:25,875 --> 00:17:30,794
Repeat for every child; one approved
sibling does not automatically verify

215
00:17:30,807 --> 00:17:35,712
another. If something is wrong, return that
child for correction with a clear

216
00:17:35,726 --> 00:17:39,938
note. Matching an existing pupil preserves
their history.

217
00:17:40,345 --> 00:17:44,693
A parent’s submitted details should not
silently overwrite the school’s

218
00:17:44,707 --> 00:17:46,215
authoritative records.

219
00:17:56,726 --> 00:18:00,585
Before sending access, check the email
handover route.

220
00:18:01,024 --> 00:18:05,901
The school can use the configured School O
S sender or its own approved S M T

221
00:18:05,915 --> 00:18:10,521
P connection. Saving credentials does not
prove an email has arrived;

222
00:18:10,888 --> 00:18:14,978
verify delivery to a controlled mailbox
before inviting everyone.

223
00:18:15,385 --> 00:18:19,597
New access is shared privately using the
available handover.

224
00:18:20,018 --> 00:18:24,448
New accounts receive time-limited setup
links, and existing account

225
00:18:24,461 --> 00:18:29,420
passwords are preserved. Do not show these
links or passwords on screen.

226
00:18:29,855 --> 00:18:33,130
The WhatsApp option prepares a message in
WhatsApp.

227
00:18:33,565 --> 00:18:38,116
A staff member must review it and press
Send; opening a draft is not

228
00:18:38,130 --> 00:18:42,355
delivery. Now sign in as the parent in a
separate browser.

229
00:18:42,746 --> 00:18:47,705
Confirm that both children appear, switch
between them and check the correct class

230
00:18:47,719 --> 00:18:52,450
information. If the children have student
logins, test the permitted

231
00:18:52,464 --> 00:18:57,287
family chat connections too. Finally,
confirm that this parent

232
00:18:57,301 --> 00:19:00,222
cannot open an unrelated pupil’s records.

233
00:19:00,657 --> 00:19:05,616
We have connected a family successfully
only when the intended access works and

234
00:19:05,630 --> 00:19:07,736
the unintended access is blocked.

235
00:19:18,273 --> 00:19:21,643
A genuinely new pupil follows the admission
route.

236
00:19:22,068 --> 00:19:26,661
Register the application or pupil draft,
review the information and any

237
00:19:26,674 --> 00:19:31,158
required documents, check for duplicates,
and record the school’s admission

238
00:19:31,171 --> 00:19:36,019
decision. Do not confuse a pending
application with an enrolled pupil

239
00:19:36,032 --> 00:19:38,532
who should already have unrestricted
access.

240
00:19:38,970 --> 00:19:43,563
After approval, verify the actual pupil
record, class and

241
00:19:43,576 --> 00:19:48,413
session. Then complete Family and login
setup, checking the parent’s

242
00:19:48,427 --> 00:19:52,476
authority and the child’s account
connection before sharing access.

243
00:19:52,897 --> 00:19:57,313
School staff make the admission decision;
the software connects the approved

244
00:19:57,326 --> 00:20:01,905
records and access workflow. For a large
intake, agree who

245
00:20:01,919 --> 00:20:04,989
reviews applications and who may issue
accounts.

246
00:20:05,424 --> 00:20:09,731
A clear handover between admissions and the
school administrator prevents

247
00:20:09,745 --> 00:20:12,720
unfinished records from falling between
teams.

248
00:20:23,257 --> 00:20:27,211
Return to Start my school and read the
progress shown for your school.

249
00:20:27,623 --> 00:20:31,074
Open any remaining check and see what is
still missing.

250
00:20:31,482 --> 00:20:35,748
A full progress bar means the six
foundation checks are satisfied.

251
00:20:36,183 --> 00:20:40,924
It does not prove that every subject has a
teacher or that your payments, report

252
00:20:40,938 --> 00:20:43,261
cards and external services are ready.

253
00:20:43,696 --> 00:20:47,093
Those services each need their own checks
before use.

254
00:20:47,528 --> 00:20:51,631
Once you’re ready for daily work, choose My
school day as your home.

255
00:20:52,066 --> 00:20:55,068
You can still come back to setup and More
tools.

256
00:20:55,503 --> 00:21:00,395
Next, we’ll prepare the services most
schools use regularly: attendance,

257
00:21:00,666 --> 00:21:03,397
fees, communication and reports.

258
00:21:03,788 --> 00:21:08,245
Complete the chapters that match what your
school will actually use on its first

259
00:21:08,258 --> 00:21:08,666
day.

260
00:21:19,217 --> 00:21:21,377
Let’s test a normal school morning.

261
00:21:21,803 --> 00:21:26,626
Sign in as the teacher, open pupil
attendance and choose the correct class and

262
00:21:26,640 --> 00:21:31,219
date. Mark the training entry, save, then
reopen the same

263
00:21:31,232 --> 00:21:35,213
register to verify it. Now check staff
attendance.

264
00:21:35,634 --> 00:21:39,765
A confirmed employee should be able to find
their own clock-in route and

265
00:21:39,779 --> 00:21:44,762
attendance history. HR should see the
corresponding authorised record for

266
00:21:44,775 --> 00:21:49,738
that date. If clock-in is missing, check
the employment link, active

267
00:21:49,751 --> 00:21:52,795
status, start date and account permissions.

268
00:21:53,187 --> 00:21:56,801
Creating another account is usually not the
right fix.

269
00:21:57,238 --> 00:22:01,599
Make sure the school understands its
attendance policy, approved leave,

270
00:22:01,898 --> 00:22:06,096
non-working days and the West Africa Time
date used by the platform.

271
00:22:06,518 --> 00:22:11,490
Review how unmarked past days are closed
before relying on absence reports for

272
00:22:11,504 --> 00:22:13,719
payroll or disciplinary decisions.

273
00:22:14,126 --> 00:22:18,692
A missing mark and a confirmed absence are
different operational facts.

274
00:22:29,214 --> 00:22:33,562
School fees are separate from your school’s
subscription to School O S.

275
00:22:34,001 --> 00:22:38,580
Here we’re setting a training tuition
charge for pupils, not buying a software

276
00:22:38,593 --> 00:22:41,960
plan. Create a class-specific fee plan.

277
00:22:42,370 --> 00:22:46,718
Choose the class, charge type, clear fee
title, amount,

278
00:22:47,017 --> 00:22:49,042
branch where relevant and frequency.

279
00:22:49,449 --> 00:22:53,199
Our example is seventy-five thousand naira
per term.

280
00:22:53,634 --> 00:22:56,433
Your school must use its own approved
figures.

281
00:22:56,854 --> 00:23:00,509
Save and inspect the plan before generating
invoices.

282
00:23:00,930 --> 00:23:05,822
Then choose the plan, enter a consistent
billing-period label and set the due

283
00:23:05,835 --> 00:23:10,412
date. Generate the class invoices only
after the pupil list and

284
00:23:10,425 --> 00:23:14,952
amounts have been checked. Open one invoice
and verify the pupil,

285
00:23:15,210 --> 00:23:20,183
charge, balance and status. In the parent
account, confirm that

286
00:23:20,197 --> 00:23:25,156
the correct family sees it. Use the same
exact billing-period wording

287
00:23:25,169 --> 00:23:29,898
consistently. Don’t create slightly
different period labels as a way of

288
00:23:29,911 --> 00:23:34,721
retrying a billing run; that can undermine
duplicate protection and confuse the

289
00:23:34,735 --> 00:23:35,767
school’s accounts.

290
00:23:46,308 --> 00:23:49,596
A payment claim is not the same as verified
money.

291
00:23:50,021 --> 00:23:54,654
For cash, bank transfer or POS, record the
payment with its

292
00:23:54,668 --> 00:23:57,738
invoice, amount, channel and reference.

293
00:23:58,146 --> 00:24:02,902
Reconcile it against the school’s
independent evidence before confirming it
as

294
00:24:02,915 --> 00:24:07,806
matched. For online collection, connect the
school’s own approved Pay

295
00:24:07,820 --> 00:24:12,752
stack account privately. First test the
complete flow in the provider’s

296
00:24:12,766 --> 00:24:17,603
test environment. Opening checkout or
returning to a success screen is

297
00:24:17,616 --> 00:24:21,094
not enough; the server must verify the
transaction.

298
00:24:21,529 --> 00:24:26,529
After verification, check the receipt and
invoice balance in the school view and

299
00:24:26,543 --> 00:24:31,312
the parent view. Test a failed or pending
payment too, so your team

300
00:24:31,325 --> 00:24:33,024
knows what families will see.

301
00:24:33,445 --> 00:24:37,929
For outstanding balances, use the available
follow-up options.

302
00:24:38,350 --> 00:24:42,983
Review the child, recipient, amount and
wording before sending an in-app

303
00:24:42,997 --> 00:24:45,442
message or opening a WhatsApp draft.

304
00:24:45,850 --> 00:24:49,206
Only authorised staff should access these
records.

305
00:24:49,614 --> 00:24:53,744
A recorded refund request is also not proof
that money has been

306
00:24:53,758 --> 00:24:54,627
transferred.

307
00:25:05,133 --> 00:25:08,408
Good communication starts with the right
audience.

308
00:25:08,823 --> 00:25:13,592
Open School chat, find a permitted person
by name and check their identity

309
00:25:13,605 --> 00:25:18,551
before writing. A chat is a conversation,
so keep the message simple.

310
00:25:18,986 --> 00:25:23,198
In this training school, we’ll send a short
welcome and confirm it in the

311
00:25:23,211 --> 00:25:24,828
recipient’s separate session.

312
00:25:25,220 --> 00:25:29,935
Typing indicators and reactions are useful,
but actual receipt is the

313
00:25:29,948 --> 00:25:34,652
important check. Use announcements or the
communications desk for a

314
00:25:34,665 --> 00:25:39,325
notice to a group. Review the audience and
preview the message before

315
00:25:39,339 --> 00:25:44,325
publishing. A driver’s route notice, for
example, should not require

316
00:25:44,339 --> 00:25:47,681
unrestricted private chat access to every
pupil.

317
00:25:48,089 --> 00:25:52,627
In-app delivery and external email, SMS or
WhatsApp are different

318
00:25:52,641 --> 00:25:57,543
services. Provider setup, verified
contacts, consent

319
00:25:57,652 --> 00:26:01,389
and funded provider accounts may be needed
for external delivery.

320
00:26:01,781 --> 00:26:06,333
Check the actual status rather than
assuming a saved notice reached every

321
00:26:06,347 --> 00:26:06,849
phone.

322
00:26:17,382 --> 00:26:21,037
Reports begin with the school’s approved
assessment structure.

323
00:26:21,449 --> 00:26:26,299
Open CA and exams and create the actual
components for the correct class,

324
00:26:26,598 --> 00:26:30,932
subject, session and term. Our training
example uses a

325
00:26:30,946 --> 00:26:35,702
continuous-assessment component worth forty
percent and an examination worth

326
00:26:35,715 --> 00:26:40,063
sixty percent. Each has a maximum raw mark
of one hundred.

327
00:26:40,484 --> 00:26:45,416
These are example school rules, not a
requirement for every Nigerian school.

328
00:26:45,824 --> 00:26:49,574
Enter the pupil’s raw marks against the
correct assessments.

329
00:26:49,995 --> 00:26:54,451
Seventy-five in the first component and
eighty in the second give a weighted

330
00:26:54,465 --> 00:26:59,163
result of seventy-eight. Check the
calculation, not just the saved

331
00:26:59,176 --> 00:27:03,636
marks. Submit and review the scores through
moderation using the

332
00:27:03,650 --> 00:27:08,432
authorised workflow. Before publication,
all required components and

333
00:27:08,446 --> 00:27:13,405
pupil scores must be complete, weights must
total one hundred percent, and the

334
00:27:13,419 --> 00:27:15,688
required approvals must be in place.

335
00:27:16,123 --> 00:27:18,419
We’re demonstrating one subject.

336
00:27:18,854 --> 00:27:23,528
Your school must complete its full intended
curriculum before issuing a genuine

337
00:27:23,541 --> 00:27:28,378
term report. Never add invented marks
simply to make publication

338
00:27:28,392 --> 00:27:28,976
pass.

339
00:27:39,502 --> 00:27:43,238
Now let’s prepare the actual report
families will receive.

340
00:27:43,650 --> 00:27:47,631
Open the visual report designer and choose
the correct school level.

341
00:27:48,039 --> 00:27:52,251
Arrange the sections your school needs:
identity, subjects,

342
00:27:52,455 --> 00:27:56,001
attendance, skills, comments and
signatures.

343
00:27:56,408 --> 00:27:59,588
You can drag sections or use the move
controls.

344
00:27:59,995 --> 00:28:04,669
Set the assessment weights and grade bands
to match the school’s approved policy

345
00:28:04,683 --> 00:28:06,884
and the assessments already created.

346
00:28:07,305 --> 00:28:12,196
Save the design draft. The person who
creates it cannot approve that

347
00:28:12,210 --> 00:28:16,830
same draft. A different authorised reviewer
must sign in with their own

348
00:28:16,843 --> 00:28:18,691
account and approve the design.

349
00:28:19,126 --> 00:28:23,365
This is a genuine review step, not a reason
to share passwords.

350
00:28:23,773 --> 00:28:28,297
After approval, assign the school-approved
format to the correct class.

351
00:28:28,732 --> 00:28:33,528
A saved generic template in school settings
is not enough; verify this

352
00:28:33,542 --> 00:28:35,294
operational class assignment.

353
00:28:35,702 --> 00:28:40,566
Nursery schools can use approved
developmental observations and age-
appropriate

354
00:28:40,580 --> 00:28:44,601
reports instead of forcing examination
marks onto young children.

355
00:28:45,036 --> 00:28:49,466
The report format should reflect how that
school actually assesses learning.

356
00:28:59,990 --> 00:29:04,691
Publication is the final step, after the
results and report format are

357
00:29:04,705 --> 00:29:09,570
ready. Check the class, session and term
carefully, then approve

358
00:29:09,583 --> 00:29:11,934
and publish through the authorised
workflow.

359
00:29:12,331 --> 00:29:14,614
Open the actual printable card.

360
00:29:15,005 --> 00:29:19,176
Check the school logo and name, pupil
identity, class,

361
00:29:19,448 --> 00:29:22,722
subjects, marks, comments and dates.

362
00:29:23,133 --> 00:29:27,100
Confirm that the report weights agree with
the assessment records.

363
00:29:27,521 --> 00:29:31,543
Next, open the same child’s report from the
parent account.

364
00:29:31,935 --> 00:29:36,677
Preview printing or saving as PDF, and
check page breaks and school

365
00:29:36,690 --> 00:29:41,446
branding. Do not assume the administrator’s
view proves the family view

366
00:29:41,460 --> 00:29:46,163
works. If the report is unavailable, check
publication, score

367
00:29:46,176 --> 00:29:50,837
completeness, moderation, the approved
format and the verified family

368
00:29:50,850 --> 00:29:55,562
link. Keep the report unpublished while
those issues are resolved.

369
00:29:55,956 --> 00:30:00,399
Progression decisions also need the
school’s own review; a threshold in a

370
00:30:00,412 --> 00:30:02,871
template is not automatic promotion.

371
00:30:13,412 --> 00:30:17,746
For transport, start with the driver,
vehicle, route and

372
00:30:17,759 --> 00:30:22,692
stops. Connect each participating pupil to
the right route and verify

373
00:30:22,706 --> 00:30:26,103
the family contacts and approved handover
arrangement.

374
00:30:26,497 --> 00:30:28,752
Test from the driver’s own account.

375
00:30:29,163 --> 00:30:34,041
A recorded pickup, home-bus journey, drop-
off or non-travel status

376
00:30:34,054 --> 00:30:36,405
should appear in the relevant pupil
history.

377
00:30:36,796 --> 00:30:39,432
Check the date and child before saving.

378
00:30:39,870 --> 00:30:44,557
A chat message is not a substitute for
approved collection authority, and the

379
00:30:44,571 --> 00:30:48,239
driver should use journey controls only
while safely parked.

380
00:30:48,660 --> 00:30:53,443
For boarding, define the hostels, rooms and
beds, then allocate

381
00:30:53,457 --> 00:30:57,791
pupils. Review who handles roll calls,
leave permits,

382
00:30:58,049 --> 00:31:00,155
visitors and welfare incidents.

383
00:31:00,576 --> 00:31:04,408
These services hold sensitive operational
information.

384
00:31:04,815 --> 00:31:09,530
Give staff the duties and records they
need, and verify the family-facing

385
00:31:09,544 --> 00:31:14,299
information. If your school does not run
buses or boarding, leave those

386
00:31:14,313 --> 00:31:16,446
services off and skip this chapter.

387
00:31:26,988 --> 00:31:31,947
For the library, begin with a few real
catalogue records and an accurate count of

388
00:31:31,960 --> 00:31:36,774
copies. Add the title and author, and an
ISBN where useful.

389
00:31:37,166 --> 00:31:41,840
Test lending and returning one book with a
verified borrower, then check that

390
00:31:41,854 --> 00:31:43,770
availability changes correctly.

391
00:31:44,179 --> 00:31:48,459
For the school store, use a clear product
image so families know what they’re

392
00:31:48,473 --> 00:31:53,079
choosing. Select the right item group, then
the relevant sizes,

393
00:31:53,351 --> 00:31:57,984
colours and quantities. A uniform needs
different details from a

394
00:31:57,997 --> 00:32:02,165
textbook or a snack. Check stock for each
variation.

395
00:32:02,559 --> 00:32:07,355
Don’t count the same units twice as both
total stock and additional variant

396
00:32:07,369 --> 00:32:12,182
stock. Review price and family-shop
visibility before offering the

397
00:32:12,196 --> 00:32:17,098
item. Place a training order, verify who
fulfils it and inspect

398
00:32:17,112 --> 00:32:21,924
the stock history. An order is not proof of
payment or proof that goods have

399
00:32:21,938 --> 00:32:26,883
been collected. Your store’s approval,
payment and handover steps should

400
00:32:26,897 --> 00:32:27,399
agree.

401
00:32:37,924 --> 00:32:42,000
For HR, confirm employee records, start
dates,

402
00:32:42,217 --> 00:32:45,981
departments, leave rules and payroll
responsibilities.

403
00:32:46,406 --> 00:32:50,917
Review pay figures and approvals with the
school’s finance team before running

404
00:32:50,931 --> 00:32:55,632
payroll. A working attendance screen alone
does not validate salary

405
00:32:55,645 --> 00:32:59,952
calculations. For live learning, first
verify teacher

406
00:32:59,966 --> 00:33:02,249
allocations and pupil access.

407
00:33:02,683 --> 00:33:07,493
Then test a class using the approved media
service, camera and microphone

408
00:33:07,507 --> 00:33:11,909
permissions, and the devices and networks
families will actually use.

409
00:33:12,344 --> 00:33:17,330
External services may require provider
accounts, quotas, payment

410
00:33:17,452 --> 00:33:21,800
or technical setup. Saved keys do not prove
capacity or

411
00:33:21,814 --> 00:33:26,678
delivery. Website publishing, prepaid
accounts, integrations

412
00:33:26,787 --> 00:33:31,325
and other advanced tools can be introduced
later with a named owner and a separate

413
00:33:31,338 --> 00:33:36,229
end-to-end test. A calm setup is one where
every active service has a

414
00:33:36,243 --> 00:33:38,825
purpose and somebody responsible for it.

415
00:33:49,377 --> 00:33:54,160
Your School O S subscription is the
software service, separate from the fees
you

416
00:33:54,173 --> 00:33:58,537
charge parents. Check your actual status,
pupil count,

417
00:33:58,836 --> 00:34:02,029
package, billing cycle and relevant dates.

418
00:34:02,466 --> 00:34:05,278
If you are on a trial, note when it ends.

419
00:34:05,699 --> 00:34:10,183
Review the current quote and payment
requirements before changing package or

420
00:34:10,197 --> 00:34:14,911
cycle. Use the actual figures shown for
your school; don’t copy a

421
00:34:14,925 --> 00:34:19,667
price from an old tutorial. A quote is not
a completed subscription

422
00:34:19,680 --> 00:34:24,259
payment. Before inviting everyone, decide
who will help staff and

423
00:34:24,273 --> 00:34:28,634
families with access problems, and who will
contact platform support.

424
00:34:29,069 --> 00:34:33,838
Use Get help with a clear description, date
and affected feature, without

425
00:34:33,852 --> 00:34:36,583
sending passwords or private setup links.

426
00:34:36,990 --> 00:34:41,623
Activity history can help an authorised
administrator investigate what

427
00:34:41,637 --> 00:34:46,053
changed. It supports review; it doesn’t
replace a clear school

428
00:34:46,066 --> 00:34:46,786
procedure.

429
00:34:57,337 --> 00:35:01,128
Before the whole school joins, run one
complete rehearsal.

430
00:35:01,567 --> 00:35:06,282
Use separate accounts for the
administrator, teacher, parent and any

431
00:35:06,295 --> 00:35:08,401
pupil or service staff involved.

432
00:35:08,792 --> 00:35:13,262
Check that the teacher sees the correct
class, attendance is saved, the

433
00:35:13,276 --> 00:35:17,066
employee can clock in and the parent sees
only their own children.

434
00:35:17,477 --> 00:35:20,969
Send a controlled in-app message and
confirm receipt.

435
00:35:21,390 --> 00:35:25,956
For every service you plan to use, finish
its own test: a verified

436
00:35:25,969 --> 00:35:30,195
payment and balance, a published printable
report, or a transport,

437
00:35:30,439 --> 00:35:33,415
library or store record that updates
correctly.

438
00:35:33,806 --> 00:35:38,792
Compare dashboard charts with the
underlying records; attractive totals
should

439
00:35:38,806 --> 00:35:43,551
still add up. Ask the platform operator to
confirm backups and restore

440
00:35:43,564 --> 00:35:48,483
testing, scheduled workers, private
storage, secure access and

441
00:35:48,496 --> 00:35:53,456
provider readiness. Those are operator
responsibilities, not extra

442
00:35:53,469 --> 00:35:55,942
menus a school owner needs to guess
through.

443
00:35:56,377 --> 00:36:01,254
Start with a small staff and family group,
resolve issues, then invite the

444
00:36:01,268 --> 00:36:05,952
rest in manageable batches. Keep a record
of what was tested and who

445
00:36:05,966 --> 00:36:10,833
approved it. You now have a clear path from
setup to a connected school

446
00:36:10,847 --> 00:36:15,765
day. Start with what matters today, verify
it with real workflows,

447
00:36:16,064 --> 00:36:18,564
and add the next service when your school
is ready.
